    "text": "To determine how many students did not pass their exams, we start by calculating the number of students who passed. We know that 75% of the 804 students passed their exams. Therefore, we can find the number of students who passed by multiplying 804 by 75%.\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\\[ 75\\% = 0.75 \\]\n\nNext, we multiply 804 by 0.75:\n\\[ 804 \\times 0.75 = 603 \\]\n\nSo, 603 students passed their exams. To find the number of students who did not pass, we subtract the number of students who passed from the total number of students:\n\\[ 804 - 603 = 201 \\]\n\nThus, the number of students who did not pass their exams is \\(\\boxed{201}\\).",
